    "created_at": "2023-09-20T07:26:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-20T07:26:51Z",
    "body": "You would also have to define the behavior. But if we wanted people to use these APIs we should also add constructors and modernize them a bit. It's just not clear to me they have the use that warrants such an investment. If you compare `[javascript] NodeIterator` and `[javascript] querySelector` on Stack Overflow the difference is quite stark. (There's also other drawbacks such as them executing script while traversing, making for expensive boundary hopping.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
